WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:12.790
What’s the word, son? This week on Thug Notes we gettin regicidal with Macbeth by William Shakespeare.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:21.640
After making a bitch out of their enemies, the king’s fresh generals, Macbeth and Banquo,

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.260
hit up three witches who start 
laying down some cold prophecy.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.940
Dem witches say one day Macbeth 
gonna rock the crown as king,

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:33.320
and Banquo’s blood also gonna be 
rollin on royals dubs one day.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:38.700
Macbeth all geeked up bout bein big baller, but his woman, Lady Macbeth, be all like,

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:44.080
“Why you wastin time play boy? 
You best get off yo lazy white ass and take dat sh*t.”

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:49.260
So Lady MacB convinces Macbeezy to shank King Duncan while he catchin some Z’s,

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:53.840
and lay the blame on his two chamberlains while they passed out from sippin too much drank.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.340
Macbeth straight trippin after doin the deed,

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:00.560
so his woman steps up and puts the
bloody knife on the chamberlains as evidence.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.980
When some fool Macduff finds 
the king’s dead body,

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:07.020
MacBeth mercs dem Chamberlains
so they can’t dodge the heat.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:13.810
All paranoid that somebody gonna ice them too, Duncan’s sons Malcom and Donalbain roll outta town.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:17.340
With them punks outta the way,
Macbeth becomes the king.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.940
Since the witches dun said Banquo’s 
blood gonna be kings one day,

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:26.120
Macbeth starts buggin and sends a couple hoods to gat Banquo and his boy Fleance.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:29.680
Banquo gets wrecked, but
Fleance ducks these fools.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:33.860
Later, Macbeth hollas at the three
witches, who lay down some new prophecy.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.100
First, an armored head tell him he 
best watch his boy Macduff.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:41.740
Then, a bloody child tell him that 
nobody born of a woman can touch him.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:48.119
Last, a crowned child holding a tree tells him he solid til Great Birnam trees roll up to the castle.

00:01:48.119 --> 00:01:55.079
Word comes that Macduff dun roll out to England, so Macbeth gets ice cold and kills his whole family! Damn!

00:01:55.080 --> 00:02:00.240
Later Macbeth learns that his woman done iced herself cuz she couldn’t get that blood off her hands.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:06.240
At first, Macbeth ain’t sweatin the fact that Malcom’s returned and got a swole army creepin up to the castle.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:11.840
But then he realizes the shields the army are using are from the same wood the witches warned him about.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:16.100
Oh f**k. Since Macduff heard that his 
family and castle got smoked,

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:20.220
he wanna go toe to toe with Macbeth.
On the battlefield, Macbeth says,

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:24.940
“Macduff, get off deez nuts. You were born of a woman. Can’t touch this!”

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:28.560
Turns out, Macduff’s mama had a 
C-section when he was born,

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.240
so Macduff wipes dat nasty smile off
his mug and beheads this fool.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:37.820
Then Malcom takes back his throne,
and Scotland got one less tyrant.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:47.180
This play right here is a classical tragedy about a once righteous brutha who balls till he falls.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.900
And it’s an unchecked ambition and lust for power that makes him his own antagonist.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.840
But is Macbeth really the only one to blame for havin such a boot-leg fate?

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:00.360
Cuz on the real, it was Lady Macbeth who put a fire under his ass to merc the king.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:04.720
And you could even blame the witches for feedin his ambition and givin him a big ol head.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.760
And Scottish society gotta ride the beef too. 
Back then, the main rap was

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:14.140
“you ain’t got a pair unless you grab all the power you can, no matter who you gotta kill for it."

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:17.380
So if you wanna say Macbeth got served cuz of all the people he shanked,

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:22.120
you best recognize he was gettin mad props for butcherin his enemies at the beginning of the play.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:25.720
In fact, some literary thugz say that 
Macbeth ain’t to blame at all,

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:30.300
but that fate slingin him around like a puppet, 
making him act like a serious fool.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:33.300
Just listen to how he talk bout life after his woman dies:

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.280
Cuz if Macbeth ain’t got no choice,
then all this sh*t is straight meaningless.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:55.360
Since fate, society, and Macbeth’s big-ass head layin more pressure on him than he can handle,

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:01.260
Shakespeare droppin images of clothes that don’t fit good to show how this playa livin way outta his depth.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:16.019
Hey, y’all know how to make a playa feel loved, man.

00:04:16.019 --> 00:04:19.410
So spread the love and tell yo friends!
Peace!

